.TH OROC-TOOLING-DOCTOR 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.2.1" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-tooling\-doctor \- Inspect editor setup without preparing dependencies.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc tooling doctor [options] [<project\-dir>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Inspect editor setup without preparing dependencies.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-language=<name>\fR
inspect one language family; otherwise inspect declared languages
.TP
\fB\-\-platform=<name>\fR
select the native target
.TP
\fB\-\-arch=<name>\fR
select target architecture
.TP
\fB\-\-variant=<name>\fR
select Android variant (default devDebug)
.TP
\fB\-\-prod\fR
inspect release model
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
emit the structured report instead of readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-config=<path>\fR
use an explicit oro.toml or oro.ini
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
show help
.SH NOTES
.PP
Checks project root, selected SDK, server executables, required tools and cached model freshness.
.PP
Does not install servers, generate models, run Gradle tasks or invoke preparation targets.
.PP
Returns a nonzero status when a required check fails; stale or absent models are warnings.
.PP
See docs/LANGUAGE_SERVER.md for configuration and editor examples.
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1), oroc\-tooling(1)
